<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14404" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπρῐάτην</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπριάδην</span> read by <i><span class="en">
			Rhian.
		</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>), Adv. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρίασθαι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without purchase-money,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα με . . ἐκομίσσατο Φείδων ἥρως
			ἀ.</span> (speaking of a man) <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.317
			</span></i>; so in late Prose 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥδετο ἀ. εὐωχούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Agath.
					4.22
				</span></i>
			:—also as fem. of Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπρίατος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή με ἀπριάτην περάσαϝτες</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημήτερα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				132
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμεναι . . κούρην ἀπριάτην ἀνάποινον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.99
				</span></i>
			: acc. pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπριάτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					169.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
